0..77 Comment "// The holders of the roles of inductive-recursive definitions, with a holder"
78..125 Comment "// of `E` that departs from its canonical body."
126..128 Comment "//"
129..203 Comment "// A holder takes its role only when it answers the canonical form of that"
204..260 Comment "// role. So a holder that departs from it holds no role."
261..263 Comment "//"
264..343 Comment "// The checker compares the holder of `E` with the canonical body at each code."
344..422 Comment "// The canonical `δ` case asks for a function from `a` into the family, which"
423..498 Comment "// the rest reads through its decodes. This holder asks for a function from"
499..576 Comment "// the family into `a`. The checker refuses it at `δ`, and it holds no role."
577..579 Comment "//"
580..644 Comment "// - owes: #3575 — the family a code defines, with its decoder"
645..721 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the codes and their arguments,"
722..735 Comment "//   admitted"
